Because this is a condominium, it can remain one piece of land.

313
00:31:46,740 --> 00:31:48,780
It has 21 limited common areas.

314
00:31:49,320 --> 00:31:55,600
Now, basically, the difference between a land condominium and a typical condominium is the unit is not the home.

315
00:31:55,600 --> 00:32:02,120
The unit is the postage stamp envelope that the home is available to be built in.

316
00:32:03,740 --> 00:32:14,920
So, what I'm anticipating is, is that they will consider the 21 units subject to a community water system.

317
00:32:15,060 --> 00:32:17,040
You can have as many wells as you want.

318
00:32:17,040 --> 00:32:27,020
But, they've got to play by different rules that would foreclose the ability to have protective radii on somebody else's property.

319
00:32:27,520 --> 00:32:29,360
So, that's something to stay tuned for.

320
00:32:29,740 --> 00:32:36,340
But, I would ask you to see if there's a way where you can do something different,

321
00:32:36,480 --> 00:32:43,880
so that we're not having those low radii overlap and significantly encroach on somebody else's property.

322
00:32:44,960 --> 00:32:46,720
I just don't, I don't like that.

323
00:32:46,720 --> 00:32:54,160
