00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:05,560
I was going to ask why all the wells have to be in that 50-foot buffer.

328
00:33:05,560 --> 00:33:20,020
So, the intent with this is that, yes, it's a land condominium, but the owners are very kind of strict to the point where they want the utilities to be unit specific.

329
00:33:20,020 --> 00:33:24,280
No, no sharing wells, no community water system, no sharing septics.

330
00:33:24,400 --> 00:33:33,700
They wanted a well per unit, just like it's not normal single-family dwelling, typical lots, but that's what they want it to feel like.

331
00:33:33,700 --> 00:33:55,960
And in doing so, just trying to keep the well radiuses away from the septic systems when I have such small limited common areas for each of these units to play with creates a bit of a back-and-forth game that I'm sure I'll continue to have with New Hampshire DES when they get me their first round of comments on their RFMI.

332
00:33:55,960 --> 00:34:00,700
I am completely confident that you will work it out.

333
00:34:01,200 --> 00:34:04,960
I'm just not sure it's going to work out the way that you might want it to.

334
00:34:05,680 --> 00:34:06,640
Yes, that's all.

335
00:34:06,640 --> 00:34:07,560
