866
01:07:18,880 --> 01:07:31,560
Dear members of the planning board, on behalf of the owner and applicant, Mark Caladare, a waiver is respectfully requested from Section 923, the Town of Sandown subdivision regulations, requiring the provision of on-site recreational facilities.

867
01:07:31,560 --> 01:07:42,840
The proposed subdivision will create one new residential lot, providing recreational facilities within these private residential lots would offer little or no practical benefit to the general public.

868
01:07:42,840 --> 01:07:53,440
The property is accessed from a class 6 road that is not maintained by the town and is not readily accessible or appropriate for public recreational use.

869
01:07:53,440 --> 01:08:05,660
Establishing a public or shared recreational area in this location would also create unnecessary access, maintenance, security, and liability concerns for the future private property owners.

870
01:08:06,380 --> 01:08:16,440
Strict compliance with Section 923 would therefore not accomplish the regulations and intended public purpose under the particular conditions of this property.

871
01:08:16,440 --> 01:08:35,300
A voluntary contribution to the Town of Sandown's Recreation Revolving Fund would provide a more practical and meaningful public benefit by allowing the Town to apply the funds towards recreational facilities that are appropriately located, publicly accessible, and maintained for public use.

872
01:08:35,960 --> 01:08:43,080
Accordingly, the applicant proposes a voluntary contribution of $1,000 for the one new residential lot created by the subdivision.

873
01:08:43,080 --> 01:08:49,860
The contribution would be paid at the time of a certificate of occupancy is issued for the new dwelling.

874
01:08:50,040 --> 01:08:53,580
The existing lot and dwelling would not be subject to any additional contribution.

875
01:08:54,780 --> 01:09:10,180
Granting this waiver would remain consistent with the spirit and intent of the subdivision regulations, would not be contrary to the public interest, and would provide a more effective recreational benefit to the Town than requiring an isolated recreational area on private property accessed by a class 6 road.

876
01:09:10,180 --> 01:09:15,940
For these reasons, the applicant respectfully requests the Planning Board approve the waiver from Section 923.

877
01:09:16,740 --> 01:09:17,460
Signed to me.

878
01:09:18,580 --> 01:09:19,260
Thank you.

879
01:09:21,220 --> 01:09:22,020
