But where does it say in the law or anywhere in the town?

916
01:11:14,020 --> 01:11:15,640
It's a voluntary contribution.

917
01:11:16,120 --> 01:11:17,040
Voluntary contribution.

918
01:11:17,040 --> 01:11:26,620
But optically, if I sat in front of a board and said, I'm going to voluntarily give you a million dollars so if I can build this nuclear reactor, it's voluntary.

919
01:11:26,740 --> 01:11:28,540
You can take a million dollars, but that looks really bad.

920
01:11:28,540 --> 01:11:34,420
So, like, where does it say in law that we can accept this money?

921
01:11:34,420 --> 01:11:35,360
I'm okay with the waiver.

922
01:11:35,580 --> 01:11:38,060
I would rather us not take any money for the waiver.

923
01:11:39,560 --> 01:11:41,160
Just give them the waiver without $1,000.

924
01:11:41,460 --> 01:11:46,420
Yeah, is there language in the bylaws that says that in exchange that you can pay a fee to waive it?

925
01:11:46,420 --> 01:11:47,680
Because I can't find it.

926
01:11:47,680 --> 01:11:54,040
As a general rule, on one or two or three house lot, we have not been taking the money.

927
01:11:54,120 --> 01:11:58,200
But people want to give us the money because they have faith in our town.

928
01:11:59,760 --> 01:12:02,100
And the need is always there.

929
01:12:02,500 --> 01:12:03,840
Well, I hear that.

930
01:12:04,080 --> 01:12:06,200
It doesn't cost the taxpayers money.

931
01:12:06,200 --> 01:12:09,320
It's not an impact fee, right?

932
01:12:10,020 --> 01:12:10,520
I know.

933
01:12:10,760 --> 01:12:12,640
It's something paid in the alternative.

934
01:12:12,900 --> 01:12:15,780
And from time to time, we have larger developments.

935
01:12:15,920 --> 01:12:26,020
It's been a while since we've had one where there is actually betterments constructed when it's appropriate, particularly in our 55 and olders, right?

936
01:12:26,480 --> 01:12:26,840
I agree.

937
01:12:26,840 --> 01:12:28,600
No, I'm all for it.

938
01:12:28,920 --> 01:12:30,060
I'm all for it.

939
01:12:30,560 --> 01:12:41,760
But we should have it in the ordinances that says if you get granted this waiver, it can be for $1,000 or $500 or $10,000.

940
01:12:42,600 --> 01:12:44,360
Then it wouldn't be voluntary, Brian.

941
01:12:44,580 --> 01:12:49,640
But if it's voluntary, who's to say that we're not taking it and giving them the waiver in exchange for $1,000?

942
01:12:50,060 --> 01:12:51,640
We're going to have to do a rational nexus.

943
01:12:51,800 --> 01:12:53,460
I say we get rid of the money altogether.

944
01:12:53,460 --> 01:12:56,960
I know it comes into the town, but optically—

945
01:12:56,960 --> 01:13:00,440
I think you might want to have an opportunity to have a conversation with somebody from the rec commission

946
01:13:00,440 --> 01:13:04,040
and how important that money is for their operations, Ed, right?

947
01:13:04,560 --> 01:13:04,840
Yes.

948
01:13:05,040 --> 01:13:06,320
Actually, they'd like more money.

949
01:13:07,260 --> 01:13:08,520
Yeah, that's what I think.

950
01:13:08,580 --> 01:13:09,680
If I was going to have a couple of dollars.

951
01:13:09,680 --> 01:13:14,480
I think we're going to have a sense for the public interest, which is precisely what 923 is about.

952
01:13:14,580 --> 01:13:21,640
So there must be a way to take it out of this conversation and put it into them just on their own going about it.

953
01:13:21,640 --> 01:13:23,600
It shouldn't even enter in our conversation.

954
01:13:23,600 --> 01:13:28,080
So perhaps we should have a future discussion about the fees.

955
01:13:29,280 --> 01:13:31,500
Well, it's not a fee, right?

956
01:13:31,600 --> 01:13:32,420
So we can't call it—

957
01:13:32,420 --> 01:13:32,740
It's voluntary.

958
01:13:32,740 --> 01:13:33,380
That's what they're saying.

959
01:13:33,720 --> 01:13:36,580
Mr. Chairman, do you want to weigh in on this?

960
01:13:37,800 --> 01:13:38,880
He's a member of the public.

961
01:13:38,880 --> 01:13:40,280
He's a member of the public.

962
01:13:40,280 --> 01:13:40,540
Oh, yeah.

963
01:13:41,460 --> 01:13:43,960
Member of the public, do you want to weigh in on this?

964
01:13:43,960 --> 01:13:46,720
Yeah, John White, David Lane, stand down.

965
01:13:46,880 --> 01:13:47,920
How's everybody doing?

966
01:13:49,440 --> 01:13:58,380
You know, where I made a suggestion at a previous hearing that we would continue the recreation donation discussion until later in this meeting,

967
01:13:59,080 --> 01:14:07,960
and where this is such a small subdivision, is this something they're trying to get approval for tonight?

968
01:14:07,960 --> 01:14:09,120
It is.

969
01:14:09,320 --> 01:14:09,920
Yes, please.

970
01:14:10,100 --> 01:14:18,960
I would say probably the smartest thing, where it is so small, maybe just granting the waiver without any type of a donation on this particular application,

971
01:14:20,160 --> 01:14:27,940
unless the applicant wanted to hold off on it, until the board itself can kind of clarify how we're operating with the recreation donation,

972
01:14:28,800 --> 01:14:30,500
or waivers with the recreation.

973
01:14:30,500 --> 01:14:39,640
I think the ongoing debate back and forth, especially at ground zero, with some members that haven't been a part of this for a long time,

974
01:14:40,200 --> 01:14:44,740
might be better served outside of a public hearing, an applicant's public hearing, you know?

975
01:14:45,540 --> 01:14:54,000
But to your point, John, I think anybody could grant, make a donation any time to the Revolving Fund, right?

976
01:14:54,240 --> 01:14:54,520
Yeah.

977
01:14:54,640 --> 01:14:57,120
Yeah, any other time for whatever.

978
01:14:57,220 --> 01:14:59,060
They could do it around Christmas, Thanksgiving.

979
01:14:59,400 --> 01:14:59,800
Absolutely.

980
01:14:59,800 --> 01:15:03,260
Or just so happen, about a day before you get a CO for a house.

981
01:15:04,000 --> 01:15:04,360
Absolutely.

982
01:15:04,660 --> 01:15:08,340
You want to contribute some money to the town that you're going to have your kids in and stuff.

983
01:15:08,640 --> 01:15:10,660
I will say, just for the public record.

984
01:15:10,780 --> 01:15:12,220
You fall into that category.

985
01:15:12,300 --> 01:15:12,940
Thank you, Mr. Wake.

986
01:15:12,960 --> 01:15:14,120
I do. I live in Sandown, guys.

987
01:15:14,980 --> 01:15:18,500
I do want to say just, it's funny that we're talking about this.

988
01:15:18,600 --> 01:15:19,360
Funny but not funny.

989
01:15:19,740 --> 01:15:21,380
That we're talking about this regulation.

990
01:15:21,900 --> 01:15:24,900
Because I do a bit of work in Fremont, one town over.

991
01:15:24,900 --> 01:15:38,180
And their planner was very interested in this procedure and this concept that we're doing to try to get recreational funds into Fremont for what Eddie talked about.

992
01:15:38,180 --> 01:15:44,320
And thought that it was a great idea to do it for every house that gets built or however they make it look.

993
01:15:44,320 --> 01:15:51,920
We sent Fremont the ordinance that you guys have in your regulations to try to implement something similar.

994
01:15:51,920 --> 01:15:56,720
Because stagnation and, you know, it's...

995
01:15:56,720 --> 01:15:59,320
I'm guilty of starting this about 20-something years ago.

996
01:15:59,480 --> 01:16:02,820
That's why we have a recreation building that we would not have today.

997
01:16:04,420 --> 01:16:06,140
Well, I think there's a huge benefit.

998
01:16:06,320 --> 01:16:08,620
I mean, we talk about things offline.

999
01:16:08,740 --> 01:16:15,700
I think my concern is the optics of it, right, looks like it's not a voluntary contribution.

1000
01:16:15,700 --> 01:16:18,600
Because you're saying, oh, well, we'll give you the waiver in exchange for the money.

1001
01:16:18,600 --> 01:16:20,200
So, objectively, it looks terrible.

1002
01:16:20,580 --> 01:16:25,000
But I also think $1,000 these days, like, that might have been great years ago.

1003
01:16:25,080 --> 01:16:27,240
But I don't know what $1,000 is going to cover now.

1004
01:16:27,500 --> 01:16:29,220
So I think that's worth a conversation.

1005
01:16:30,260 --> 01:16:33,620
If the idea is to give a waiver because they don't need to...

1006
01:16:33,620 --> 01:16:36,440
And this application is completely different.

1007
01:16:36,580 --> 01:16:39,900
No, and I don't mind talking about it at all, too, because I'm a Sandown resident.

1008
01:16:40,240 --> 01:16:46,380
And I care about what you guys are talking about, regardless, outside of the application that I'm representing.

1009
01:16:46,380 --> 01:16:48,720
So I don't mind it being talked about.

1010
01:16:49,000 --> 01:16:52,300
But I do agree that maybe a bigger conversation is needed.

1011
01:16:52,660 --> 01:16:53,640
I definitely think so.

1012
01:16:53,720 --> 01:16:58,460
And I think this application is separate from the bigger conversation, for sure.

1013
01:16:59,160 --> 01:17:04,060
Because I think if we're looking at what the point of this language is, is to, you know,

1014
01:17:04,140 --> 01:17:08,720
they're either building kind of their own recreation or they're kind of contributing into town.

1015
01:17:08,820 --> 01:17:12,960
If they're going to contribute into town, then that should be a worthwhile amount, right,

1016
01:17:12,980 --> 01:17:15,300
that we can do something to this town with, right?

1017
01:17:15,300 --> 01:17:17,480
Perhaps we build more recreation things.

1018
01:17:17,600 --> 01:17:21,800
Perhaps we put more things into town for the people that are coming in and building more homes.

1019
01:17:21,860 --> 01:17:26,580
I think this is an opportunity for us to say, okay, we're going to bring more people in, more houses in,

1020
01:17:26,640 --> 01:17:30,700
but let's make sure that we add more to the resources, the revolving fund,

1021
01:17:30,860 --> 01:17:32,860
to make sure that it accommodates these people.

1022
01:17:33,360 --> 01:17:34,240
That's what this does.

1023
01:17:34,740 --> 01:17:36,580
I just don't think $1,000 does it.

1024
01:17:36,800 --> 01:17:37,760
$1,000 is nothing.

1025
01:17:37,760 --> 01:17:40,080
Okay, can we, we have a motion.

1026
01:17:40,700 --> 01:17:42,300
Eddie, would you want to repeat the motion?

1027
01:17:43,040 --> 01:17:44,760
And then we'll vote on this motion.

1028
01:17:44,880 --> 01:17:45,940
If it passes, it passes.

1029
01:17:46,040 --> 01:17:47,520
If it doesn't pass, it doesn't pass.

1030
01:17:48,020 --> 01:17:55,100
And we'll make a motion to give the waiver to 9.23 on-site recreation,

1031
01:17:55,100 --> 01:18:02,040
property 25 Hershey Road, tax map 12, Lauday, $1,000 donation.

1032
01:18:02,380 --> 01:18:05,380
Donate, $1,000 voluntary donation.

1033
01:18:05,640 --> 01:18:06,240
Voluntary donation.

1034
01:18:06,340 --> 01:18:08,400
To the revolving recreation fund.

1035
01:18:08,420 --> 01:18:09,300
Thank you for the verbiage.

1036
01:18:11,200 --> 01:18:12,200
Do I have a second?

1037
01:18:15,500 --> 01:18:16,600
Yeah, I'll second it.

1038
01:18:16,600 --> 01:18:23,020
All right, all those in favor to accept this donation.

1039
01:18:24,460 --> 01:18:31,540
Okay, we have four, four, four, Matt, myself, Ed, and Liam.

1040
01:18:32,040 --> 01:18:34,900
All those against, all those abstaining.

1041
01:18:38,620 --> 01:18:39,420
Okay.

1042
01:18:40,380 --> 01:18:41,300
So 501.

1043
01:18:41,320 --> 01:18:41,760
Help me out.

1044
01:18:42,500 --> 01:18:42,940
Brian.

1045
01:18:43,300 --> 01:18:43,820
Brian.

1046
01:18:44,520 --> 01:18:45,120
Thank you, Brian.

1047
01:18:45,120 --> 01:18:45,400
And Lisa.

1048
01:18:45,400 --> 01:18:46,700
Oh, I voted.

1049
01:18:47,480 --> 01:18:48,160
Oh, you voted too?

1050
01:18:48,440 --> 01:18:49,300
I didn't see your hand.

1051
01:18:49,860 --> 01:18:51,620
Okay, so everybody.

1052
01:18:52,000 --> 01:18:52,480
Not very big.

1053
01:18:52,500 --> 01:18:53,700
Brian's the only one that abstained.

1054
01:18:53,880 --> 01:18:54,100
Okay.

1055
01:18:54,660 --> 01:18:54,960
Awesome.

1056
01:18:55,240 --> 01:18:56,200
Thank you, board.

1057
01:18:56,300 --> 01:18:56,640
You're welcome.

1058
01:18:58,540 --> 01:18:59,400
Let's see here.

1059
01:19:00,880 --> 01:19:01,440
All right.

1060
01:19:01,920 --> 01:19:05,880
So do we have some questions on this subdivision?

1061
01:19:07,080 --> 01:19:07,980
It's pretty easy.

1062
01:19:08,280 --> 01:19:09,600
You have a list of things, right?

1063
01:19:09,600 --> 01:19:09,920
Yeah.

1064
01:19:11,580 --> 01:19:13,780
Anybody from the board have any questions?

1065
01:19:13,780 --> 01:19:22,720
So one driveway is coming off of a private right-of-way, and that's the long driveway we've been talking,

1066
01:19:23,040 --> 01:19:25,340
that we have to get clarified from the fire chief?

1067
01:19:25,840 --> 01:19:35,900
Yeah, and as Steve kind of alluded to, that is more of an occupancy, police chief kind of life safety matter, in a way.

1068
01:19:35,900 --> 01:19:46,220
I don't think it's really – what he may change is where he would like the turnaround and how big it is at the time of construction.

1069
01:19:46,860 --> 01:19:51,960
You know, once they start cutting trees out here and the house actually goes in and we know that the garage is facing this way,

1070
01:19:51,960 --> 01:19:55,860
it might change where it's going to go, you know?

1071
01:19:56,040 --> 01:20:03,540
If you take a look at the drawings, Ernie, there's an existing Woods Road on the property.

1072
01:20:04,020 --> 01:20:04,180
Yeah.

1073
01:20:04,180 --> 01:20:08,060
That actually shows up on Ryan's plan, existing –

1074
01:20:08,060 --> 01:20:08,760
Yeah, on sheet one.

1075
01:20:09,840 --> 01:20:09,980
Yeah.

1076
01:20:10,160 --> 01:20:11,300
You can see where the –

1077
01:20:11,300 --> 01:20:12,600
It shows up on both, actually.

1078
01:20:12,680 --> 01:20:12,860
Yeah.

1079
01:20:12,860 --> 01:20:14,000
That's the existing one.

1080
01:20:14,240 --> 01:20:19,940
Oh, that – and with – that's not where the – that's the existing – the IRS here is the existing –

1081
01:20:19,940 --> 01:20:20,820
It's existing.

1082
01:20:21,040 --> 01:20:21,540
It's there.

1083
01:20:21,740 --> 01:20:25,560
You know, it's obviously not to the standard that you would have to build a house or anything.

1084
01:20:25,560 --> 01:20:35,440
But you remember when the subdivision next door was done and they created the private way, Cronin's Landing,

1085
01:20:36,420 --> 01:20:48,340
they put in the box culvert that Ryan talked about, there is at least casual easement rights over the Cronin property for the benefit of this –

1086
01:20:48,340 --> 01:20:49,120
Piece of –

1087
01:20:49,120 --> 01:20:49,360
Yep.

1088
01:20:49,360 --> 01:21:00,280
So, we compelled at the time, and it was a good idea for a bunch of reasons, including, as Ryan indicated tonight,

1089
01:21:02,020 --> 01:21:07,420
alleviation of need for additional future wetlands impacts if and when something happened on this property.

1090
01:21:07,760 --> 01:21:07,980
Yep.

1091
01:21:08,440 --> 01:21:15,720
So that the private way that is Cronin's Landing immediately abuts the property line.

1092
01:21:15,720 --> 01:21:21,080
And so, we set this up for this to happen.

1093
01:21:21,780 --> 01:21:22,140
Okay.

1094
01:21:22,400 --> 01:21:23,120
If you remember.

1095
01:21:23,360 --> 01:21:24,560
I kind of do remember, yeah.

1096
01:21:25,080 --> 01:21:33,860
So, it was environmentally a good thing to do, and where it kicks in is where this existing woods road feeds off

1097
01:21:33,860 --> 01:21:38,560
and goes up to the crest of the hill where the logical building site is on the site, on the property.

1098
01:21:38,560 --> 01:21:45,840
So, NFPA1 kicks in, and Mike is the authority having to do this.

1099
01:21:47,840 --> 01:21:52,780
You know, there's different NFPA1 requirements, as some of you know.

1100
01:21:52,860 --> 01:22:03,140
I think many of you know, for driveways, once you reach 150 feet in length, and then, again, at 300 feet, over 300 feet.

1101
01:22:03,140 --> 01:22:13,700
This is of the ladder category, and Mike can ask for things like a turnaround that he can't ask.

1102
01:22:13,820 --> 01:22:15,860
It was 299 feet long.

1103
01:22:16,000 --> 01:22:16,940
He can't ask for it.

1104
01:22:16,940 --> 01:22:27,040
So, until we really have a building plan, you know, and Mike has to sign off on the issues of any building permits that Jason may issue,

1105
01:22:27,520 --> 01:22:34,540
the logical time to have this conversation is when somebody knows who's going to build, when, and what, right?

1106
01:22:34,540 --> 01:22:45,200
So, for that reason, if you look at the text of Note 24 on Sheet 1 of the drawings that Ryan added to the plan,

1107
01:22:45,320 --> 01:22:47,600
it pretty much captures all of that, right?

1108
01:22:47,860 --> 01:22:52,380
They may not have that one because of the updates that I've had to do because of your letter.

1109
01:22:52,940 --> 01:22:56,180
I can read, so Note 24 that the board probably does not have, correct?

1110
01:22:56,960 --> 01:22:57,940
It's on the plan here.

1111
01:22:58,540 --> 01:23:01,400
You have the proposed driveway serving?

1112
01:23:01,920 --> 01:23:02,140
Is that?

1113
01:23:02,480 --> 01:23:02,680
Yep.

1114
01:23:02,680 --> 01:23:03,680
Okay, you guys have it then.

1115
01:23:03,720 --> 01:23:03,820
Okay.

1116
01:23:03,820 --> 01:23:06,220
Maybe Andrea made it for him.

1117
01:23:06,320 --> 01:23:06,700
She did.

1118
01:23:07,860 --> 01:23:08,540
She's the best.

1119
01:23:08,560 --> 01:23:10,760
Remember, she's done this job before.

1120
01:23:11,440 --> 01:23:12,280
You don't say.

1121
01:23:14,560 --> 01:23:14,920
Capably.

1122
01:23:15,900 --> 01:23:18,820
She could have asked me to make some, but she's sweet.

1123
01:23:21,940 --> 01:23:22,700
She's very good.

1124
01:23:22,720 --> 01:23:25,600
I was thinking you guys were looking at an older version of the plan the whole time.

1125
01:23:26,220 --> 01:23:28,320
And any other driveway is just coming off of Hershey Road?

1126
01:23:28,880 --> 01:23:30,000
Yeah, and it exists.

1127
01:23:30,340 --> 01:23:30,520
Yeah.

1128
01:23:30,780 --> 01:23:30,920
Yeah.

1129
01:23:31,420 --> 01:23:33,480
You guys been up to Hershey, that area?

1130
01:23:33,480 --> 01:23:33,940
At all?

1131
01:23:34,940 --> 01:23:36,000
It's really nice.

1132
01:23:36,520 --> 01:23:42,100
They've done a good job at reclaiming the section of the road all the way up to where this is going to be.

1133
01:23:42,240 --> 01:23:43,180
So there's really no.

1134
01:23:43,580 --> 01:23:44,900
Some beautiful houses up there.

1135
01:23:44,900 --> 01:23:54,320
Yeah, and if you really couldn't benefit any more from having a Manning live across the street from you who owns a construction company.

1136
01:23:54,520 --> 01:23:54,760
Right?

1137
01:23:54,940 --> 01:23:55,080
Yeah.

1138
01:23:55,160 --> 01:23:56,320
Takes good care of the road.

1139
01:23:56,580 --> 01:23:57,220
Matt Manning.

1140
01:23:57,420 --> 01:23:57,560
Yeah.

1141
01:23:57,720 --> 01:23:58,660
Matt's a great guy.

1142
01:23:58,660 --> 01:23:59,160
All right.

1143
01:23:59,160 --> 01:24:02,160
All right.

1144
01:24:04,160 --> 01:24:05,640
So you're okay with this, Steve?

1145
01:24:06,540 --> 01:24:09,060
Well, I mean, I got the letter I had summarized.

1146
01:24:09,060 --> 01:24:09,560
You know?

1147
01:24:09,560 --> 01:24:10,800
So we could do a conditional.

1148
01:24:10,800 --> 01:24:18,440
Well, if the Chair were to entertain a motion for approval, these are the conditions I would recommend.

1149
01:24:18,440 --> 01:24:29,500
One, demonstration of availability of easement rights to permit driveway access to future law 8-1 via Cronus Landing, a private way.

1150
01:24:31,580 --> 01:24:42,900
Receipt two, receipt of correspondence from myself confirming comments and recommendations offered in letter report dated September 25th, 2026, have been resolved.

